{
  "slug": "js_math",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 79,
  "url": "/js/js_math.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Math Object",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Math Object"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Math Object"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The JavaScript Math object allows you to perform mathematical tasks."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The Math object is static."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "All methods and properties can be used without creating a Math object first."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.PI;"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Try it Yourself »"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math Properties (Constants)"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The syntax for any Math property is : Math.property."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript provides 8 mathematical constants that can be accessed as Math properties:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.E        // returns Euler's number\n\nMath.PI       // returns PI\n\nMath.SQRT2    // returns the square root of 2\n\nMath.SQRT1_2  // returns the square root of 1/2\n\nMath.LN2      // returns the natural logarithm of 2\n\nMath.LN10     // returns the natural logarithm of 10\n\nMath.LOG2E    // returns base 2 logarithm of E\n\nMath.LOG10E   // returns base 10 logarithm of E",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_constants"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The syntax for Math any methods is : Math.method(number)"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Number to Integer"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "There are 4 common methods to round a number to an integer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Math.round(x)", "Returns x rounded to its nearest integer"],
        ["Math.ceil(x)", "Returns x rounded up to its nearest integer"],
        ["Math.floor(x)", "Returns x rounded down to its nearest integer"],
        ["Math.trunc(x)", "Returns the integer part of x (new in ES6)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.round()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.round(x) returns the nearest integer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.round(4.6);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.round(4.5);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.round(4.4);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_round_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.ceil()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.ceil(x) returns the value of x rounded up to its nearest integer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.ceil(4.9);\n\nMath.ceil(4.7);\n\nMath.ceil(4.4);\n\nMath.ceil(4.2);\n\nMath.ceil(-4.2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_ceil"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.floor()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.floor(x) returns the value of x rounded down to its nearest integer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.floor(4.9);\n\nMath.floor(4.7);\n\nMath.floor(4.4);\n\nMath.floor(4.2);\n\nMath.floor(-4.2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_floor"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.trunc()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.trunc(x) returns the integer part of x:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.trunc(4.9);\n\nMath.trunc(4.7);\n\nMath.trunc(4.4);\n\nMath.trunc(4.2);\n\nMath.trunc(-4.2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_trunc"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.sign()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.sign(x) returns if x is negative, null or positive."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "If x is positive it returns 1",
        "If x is negative it returns -1",
        "If x is zero, it returns 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.sign(-4);\n\nMath.sign(0);\n\nMath.sign(4);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_sign"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.trunc() and Math.sign() were added to JavaScript 2015 - ES6."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.pow()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.pow(x, y) returns the value of x to the power of y:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.pow(8, 2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_pow"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.sqrt()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.sqrt(x) returns the square root of x:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.sqrt(64);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_sqrt"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.abs()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.abs(x) returns the absolute (positive) value of x:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.abs(-4.7);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_abs"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.sin()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.sin(x) returns the sine (a value between -1 and 1) of the angle x (given in radians)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you want to use degrees instead of radians, you have to convert degrees to radians:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Angle in radians = Angle in degrees x PI / 180."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.sin(90 * Math.PI / 180);     // returns 1 (the sine of 90 degrees)",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_sin"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.cos()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.cos(x) returns the cosine (a value between -1 and 1) of the angle x (given in radians)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you want to use degrees instead of radians, you have to convert degrees to radians:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Angle in radians = Angle in degrees x PI / 180."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.cos(0 * Math.PI / 180);     // returns 1 (the cos of 0 degrees)",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_cos"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.min() and Math.max()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.min() and Math.max() can be used to find the lowest or highest value in a list of arguments:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.min(0, 150, 30, 20, -8, -200);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_min"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.max(0, 150, 30, 20, -8, -200);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_max"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Math.random()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.random() returns a random number between 0 (inclusive), and 1\n(exclusive):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.random();",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_random"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "You will learn more about Math.random() in the next chapter of this tutorial."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Math.log() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.log(x) returns the natural logarithm of x."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The natural logarithm returns the time needed to reach a certain level of growth:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log(1);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log(2);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log(3);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_log"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.E and Math.log() are twins."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log(10);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_log_ten_times"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Math.log2() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.log2(x) returns the base 2 logarithm of x."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log2(8);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_log2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Math.log10() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Math.log10(x) returns the base 10 logarithm of x."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Math.log10(1000);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_math_log10"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Learn More:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Full Math Reference"
    }
  ]
}
